mma for alpha=2 and alpha=4, using the analytic RILW model.","readouts":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":441,"line_start":439,"support":"MSD scales as t^gamma(alpha) for t->infinity, implying MSD(t)/MSD(t_ref) = (t/t_ref)^gamma."}],"definition":"Normalized MSD scaling ratio M(r) = MSD(r*t_ref)/MSD(t_ref) = r^gamma, defined as the limit t_ref -> infinity at fixed r.","name":"M","resolution":null,"statistic":"Asymptotic scaling ratio derived from the power-law MSD; not a finite-sample average.","uncertainty":"source_unspecified","unit":"dimensionless"}],"source":{"arxiv_versioned_id":"2503.15027v1","citation":"Soma Shiraki, Tunable Anomalous Diffusion in Subrecoil-Laser-Cooled Atoms, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/9pb2-v6zs","journal_doi":"10.1103/9pb2-v6zs"},"source_ambiguities":[]}
